text:
kelly (Design): Quick accessibility sweep: noticed the focus outline for the Alerts bell in compact header is almost invisible in Light theme and VoiceOver reads the bell label twice when toggling the panel. Can we triage?
raj (Frontend): Thanks — repro steps? I suspect two things: 1) the focus is using a subtle 1px border that blends with BG, 2) the panel unmounts during close animation which can cause tab order and SR duplication.
kelly (Design): Steps: Tab to bell -> Space to open -> Tab -> focus sometimes jumps to search input instead of panel first item. VoiceOver reads "Alerts, button" then "Alerts" again. Screenshot attached.
sam (A11y): Initial notes: - Focus visibility: make focus an obvious cue (recommend 3px outline or >=2px solid with offset) and avoid color-only cues. Use `prefers-contrast: more` to increase thickness. - Panel behavior: keep the panel mounted during animation (don't remove from DOM) or use a focus trap while panel open. - SR duplication likely from live region + aria-expanded toggles; remove unnecessary `aria-live` or consolidate announcement. - Use `aria-expanded` on trigger, `aria-controls` linking to panel, and `role=\"dialog\"` or `menu` as appropriate.
ivy (QA): Can repro on macOS & Windows. NVDA shows similar duplicate announcement. I'll add a small screencap. I'll write an e2e: tab to bell, open panel, assert focus lands on first actionable item and Shift+Tab returns to bell. Also check that VoiceOver reads single announcement.
raj (Frontend): Quick CSS stopgap:
```
.header .bell:focus {
  outline: 3px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
  .header .bell:focus { outline-width: 4px; }
}
```
JS: keep panel DOM mounted with `data-closing` until `transitionend` and call `focus()` on the first focusable on open. Will prototype and post screenshots.
kelly (Design): Neutral outline OK for the quick patch. We'll revisit accent usage once we have a handful of fixes across the header. Please respect reduced-motion.
sam (A11y): Also add a small SR smoke test asserting no duplicate announcements and include `prefers-reduced-motion` handling. Consider roving tabindex patterns if the panel is a menu.
ivy (QA): I'll add the Cypress test and run VoiceOver/NVDA smoke on staging once PR lands. Marking P2 for now.
raj (Frontend): I'll open WIP PR 2197 with CSS, JS, and the e2e. Tagging @kelly and @sam for review.
deploy-bot: staging deploy scheduled for PR 2197 at 21:00 UTC
kelly (Design): Decision for patch: 1) implement neutral 3px outline for bell focus, 2) keep panel mounted during animations + focus management, 3) add prefers-contrast & reduced-motion tweaks. Follow-up: audit other header controls next sprint.
sam (A11y): :thumbsup: please add a release-note blurb and include the accessibility checklist entry.
ivy (QA): I'll run the SR smoke after deploy and report results here.
